document, and renames the now-unused `permit` parameter to `_permit` per AC-020. AC-006 (signature identity) is verified by the crate continuing to compile with every existing call site of write_version unchanged in argument count/type/order. This task's own new test proves the general AC-002 claim (mutate alone doesn't touch disk, persist afterward flushes) with a plain, non-workspace fixture; the workspace-inherited-version branch's OWN AC-002 proof is added in T05b -- so AC-002 is jointly covered by T05a and T05b. AC-015: this task inserts persist() at 4 of cargo.rs's 8 total disk-reading call sites (the 4 ordinary write_version sites); the 5th write_version site (the workspace-inheriting test) is T05b's, and the remaining 3 (update_dependency_spec) are T06's.

