  "reasoning": "Moved to land immediately after T01a/T01b and before the apply.rs wiring tasks (T03/T04) and the mutator-stripping tasks (T05a onward), per round-3 fix (4): T04 (rewrites-loop wiring) adds an unconditional handle.persist(permit)? after update_dependency_spec; without this guard already in place, the narrow self-referential CargoToml delegation case (handle's own path equals workspace_root.join("Cargo.toml")) would let that unconditional persist silently revert the delegation's write for the commits between T04 and this task landing -- a real hazard, not a provably-harmless one (unlike the ordinary delegation/no-op cases documented in non_goals item 1 and covered by AC-008 case 1 / AC-013). This task's own red phase is independent of any stripping task -- it is a genuine compile error (E0599, missing InvariantViolation variant) followed by a genuine new-behavior assertion (a previously-silent delegation now returns an error) -- so it is free to move to the front of the sequence. The variant is added here rather than in T01a because it has exactly one caller and belongs with it.",
  "failing_test": "Add to crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs's `mod tests` (needs `use std::sync::Arc;`, already imported at file scope and visible via `use super::*;`):
```rust
#[test]
fn update_dependency_spec_self_referential_workspace_delegation_returns_invariant_violation() {
    let dir = tempdir().unwrap();
    let root_cargo_path = dir.path().join("Cargo.toml");
    let content = "[workspace]\nmembers = [\".\"]\n\n[package]\nname = \"self-referential-root\"\nversion = \"1.0.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[dependencies]\nserde = { workspace = true }\n\n[workspace.dependencies]\nserde = \"1.0.0\"\n";
    fs::write(&root_cargo_path, content).unwrap();

    let inheritance = WorkspaceCargoResolver::load(&root_cargo_path)
        .unwrap()
        .inheritance()
        .unwrap();

    let decl = ManifestDecl::new(
        "Cargo.toml",
        ManifestRole::Canonical,
        ManifestFormat::CargoToml,
    )
    .unwrap();
    let ctx = OpenContext {
        workspace_root: dir.path(),
        cargo_workspace: Some(Arc::new(inheritance)),
        npm_workspace_kind: None,
    };

    let mut manifest = CargoToml::open(&decl, &ctx).unwrap();

    let new_spec = DepSpec::Range(
        VersionReq::parse("^1.1.0", Ecosystem::Cargo).unwrap(),
        "^1.1.0".to_string(),
    );
    let result = manifest.update_dependency_spec(
        "serde",
        callisto_model::DepKind::Runtime,
        new_spec,
        &permit(),
    );

    assert!(
        matches!(result, Err(ManifestError::InvariantViolation { .. })),
        "expected InvariantViolation, got: {result:?}"
    );

    let on_disk = fs::read_to_string(&root_cargo_path).unwrap();
    assert_eq!(on_disk, content, "manifest file must be unchanged on disk");

    manifest.persist(&permit()).unwrap();
    let after_persist = fs::read_to_string(&root_cargo_path).unwrap();
    assert_eq!(after_persist, content, "in-memory document must not have been mutated by the failed call");
}
```",
  "test_command": "cargo test -p callisto-manifests --lib cargo::tests::update_dependency_spec_self_referential_workspace_delegation_returns_invariant_violation",
  "expected_failure": "error[E0599]: no variant or associated item named `InvariantViolation` found for enum `ManifestError` in the current scope
(the crate fails to compile because ManifestError has no InvariantViolation variant yet)",
  "implementation": "In crates/callisto-model/src/error.rs, add to the end of the `ManifestError` enum (after `FormattingNotPreserved`):
```rust
    #[error("`{path}`: {message}")]
    #[diagnostic(code(E027))]
    InvariantViolation { path: PathBuf, message: String },
```
In crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs, in `update_dependency_spec`, replace:
```rust
        if self.inherited_deps.contains(&(kind, name.to_string())) {
            let root_cargo = self.workspace_root.join("Cargo.toml");
            let mut ws_res = WorkspaceCargoResolver::load(&root_cargo)?;
            return ws_res.write_dependency(name, new, permit);
        }
```
with:
```rust
        if self.inherited_deps.contains(&(kind, name.to_string())) {
            let root_cargo = self.workspace_root.join("Cargo.toml");
            if self.absolute == root_cargo {
                return Err(ManifestError::InvariantViolation {
                    path: self.path.clone(),
                    message: format!(
                        "dependency `{name}` is workspace-inherited but this manifest IS the workspace root (`{}`); refusing to delegate to avoid overwriting the just-written root manifest with a stale in-memory document",
                        root_cargo.display()
                    ),
                });
            }
            let mut ws_res = WorkspaceCargoResolver::load(&root_cargo)?;
            return ws_res.write_dependency(name, new, permit);
        }
```",
  "verify_command": "cargo test -p callisto-manifests --lib cargo::tests",
  "expected_pass": "test result: ok. 0 failed. (cargo.rs grows from 22, after T01a, to 23, the 1 new function being update_dependency_spec_self_referential_workspace_delegation_returns_invariant_violation. Absolute total is informational only -- the pass condition is 0 failed.)",
  "commit_message": "fix(manifests): guard against CargoToml self-delegation to its own workspace root

When a non-virtual workspace root manifest (both [workspace] and
[package]) tries to update one of its own workspace-inherited
dependencies, update_dependency_spec now returns
ManifestError::InvariantViolation instead of silently delegating to a
WorkspaceCargoResolver targeting the same file the caller will later
persist() over. Defensive: cascade.rs never constructs this case
today (see AC-017). Landed ahead of apply.rs's rewrites-loop persist()
wiring (T04) so that wiring can never observe the unguarded hazard."
}

